WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:00.890
The twins.

00:01.613 --> 00:07.678
Two bright stars side by side, Castor and Pollux, are the heads of twin brothers standing in the Milky Way.

00:08.187 --> 00:09.652
They only look like twins.

00:09.964 --> 00:13.144
Pollux is an orange giant thirty-four light-years away.

00:13.705 --> 00:17.870
Castor is fifty-one, and is really six stars circling one another.
